From 3113d44a1e5cd4e9ea4f3bf0200cdb46a9e5cb20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:09:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Multiple dataloaders: a share of each step per dataset, with
 async GRPO

data.num_prompts_per_dataloader takes a size per task name, and the sizes must add up to
grpo.num_prompts_per_step. Each dataset starts its next pass on its own when it runs out.

Async GRPO now accepts multiple dataloaders. The wrapper builds its iterators at the first pull, so that it
can be sent to the collector actor, its length is the pass of the longest dataset, and checkpoints keep
each dataset's position in train_dataloader_<task>.pt.

With more than one task, validation logs accuracy_<task> and training logs reward_<task>. A null
grpo.max_val_samples validates on every row.
